.SH "MIGRATION"
.SS "Migration Planning:"
.sp
Before starting the migration, familiarize yourself with saptune version 3.
Please read the man pages of \fBsaptune\fP(8) and \fBsaptune\-note\fP(5).
.sp
Solutions of version 3 can encompass more SAP Notes than in version 1.
Please check section \fBSOLUTIONS\fP for details. You might want to deselect some SAP Notes, change or disable parameters.
.sp
SAP notes are more comprehensive in version 3.
Please check section \fBSAP NOTES\fP for details. You might want to change or disable parameters.
.sp
Some SAP notes have been removed in version 3.
Please check section \fBSAP NOTES\fP for details. You might want to add your own configuration file.
.sp
In version 1 multiple solutions can be applied, in saptune version 3 only one at the same time.
If you had multiple solutions in the past, choose the most suitable one and add additional notes.
.sp
Version 1 has changed system parameters only when the current value was lower.
Version 3 will set the parameter always to the configured value, no matter the current value.
.SS "Migration Steps:"
.sp
The following steps describe the easiest way to migrate from version 1 to version 3.
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 1.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 1." 4.2
.\}
Determine current solutions and SAP Notes for version 1 and plan the ones for version 3.
.sp
Use these commands to get a list of selected solutions and notes:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
saptune solution list
saptune note list
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
Use the sections \fBSOLUTIONS\fP and \fBSAP NOTES\fP above to familiarize yourself with the changes and create a list of the solution and SAP Notes you are going to use with version 3.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 2.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 2." 4.2
.\}
(Skip, if saptune defaults are acceptable) Check each chosen SAP Note and former configuration.
.sp
Verify that the shipped defaults of version 3 meet your requirements.
.sp
\fBSince saptune is running in version 1 prior to migration you cannot use \*(Aqsaptune note show\*(Aq yet. Please check the files in /usr/share/saptune/notes/ directly.\fP
.sp
Verify the version 1 configuration (see \fBSAP NOTES\fP above) for settings to carry over.
.sp
For step 8 you need to prepare a list with all parameters that have to be added, altered or disabled.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 3.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 3." 4.2
.\}
Revert \fBall\fP solutions and notes.
.sp
Use the following commands:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
saptune solution revert <solution>
saptune note revert <note>
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
Please check if the following variables in \f(CR/etc/sysconfig/saptune\fP are empty:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
TUNE_FOR_SOLUTIONS=""
TUNE_FOR_NOTES=""
NOTE_APPLY_ORDER=""
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 4.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 4." 4.2
.\}
Change saptune version variable to "3".
.sp
Open \f(CR/etc/sysconfig/saptune\fP in an editor and set the variable \f(CRSAPTUNE_VERSION\fP from "1" to "3".
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 5.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 5." 4.2
.\}
Remove the configuration directory \f(CR/etc/tuned/saptune/\fP.
.sp
During the package upgrade a compatibility configuration \f(CR/etc/tuned/saptune/\fP was created, which has to be removed to run version 3 properly.
.sp
It is possible that it was created manually in the past to alter the configuration. In this case verify the configuration and extend your future saptune configuration (step 2). Saptune version 3 performs all tuning settings itself and no longer uses tuned for tuning.
.sp
The line \f(CR#stv1tov2#\fP is an indicator that the configuration file was created by the update process and not manually.
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04' 6.\h'+01'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP " 6." 4.2
.\}
Remove files which are not needed anymore.
.sp
\fBPlease copy each file to a safe location before deleting it! You might need it to check for former configuration values.\fP
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Delete the configuration files \f(CRSAP_BOBJ\-SAP_Business_OBJects.conf\fP and \f(CRSAP_ASE\-SAP_Adaptive_Server_Enterprise.conf\fP:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
rm /etc/saptune/extra/{SAP_BOBJ\-SAP_Business_OBJects.conf,SAP_ASE\-SAP_Adaptive_Server_Enterprise.conf}
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Delete old note configuration files:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
rm /etc/sysconfig/saptune\-note\-*
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.RE
.sp
.RS 4
.ie n \{\
\h'-04'\(bu\h'+03'\c
.\}
.el \{\
.  sp -1
.  IP \(bu 2.3
.\}
Delete \f(CR/etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/sap.conf\fP:
.sp
